**Scenario**

An item uses automatic enrollment: the customer is put on a fixed auto order schedule at checkout and does not pick a
frequency.  You want customers to be able to change the frequency of that item from MyAccount, for example to Monthly,
Every 2 Months, or every 30, 60 or 90 days.

Three properties on `item.auto_order` control this:

| Property | Type | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `auto_order_myaccount_frequency_schedules` | array of strings | Standard schedule names, e.g. `Monthly`, `Every 2 Months` |
| `auto_order_myaccount_frequency_day_counts` | array of integers | Day counts, 1 to 365, at most 20, e.g. `[30, 60, 90]`.  10, 24, 28 and 45 are saved as the standard schedules `Every 10 Days` and so on. |
| `auto_order_myaccount_frequency_last_step_only` | boolean | Only offer the change once the item is on its last auto order step |

Omit a property to leave it unchanged.  Send an empty array to clear it.  Empty schedules and day counts turn the
MyAccount frequency change off for the item.

Requirements:
- UltraCart support must enable "MyAccount - Advanced Auto Order Settings" on your account.  Without it, setting these
  properties returns a 400.
- The item must use automatic enrollment (`auto_order.auto_order_upsell` = `true`).  Otherwise a 400.
- The change is only offered to a customer when the item's auto order steps repeat forever.  An item whose steps end
  (for example "Monthly x5, then stop") never offers it, whatever is set here.  UltraCart checks this when the customer
  asks, not when you save the item.

Expansion matters here:
- Read the item with `_expand=auto_order`.  That returns the whole `auto_order` section, including these properties.
- Send that same `auto_order` object back.  When `auto_order` is present in an update, UltraCart writes every auto order
  setting from it, so a partial or hand-built `auto_order` object would reset settings you did not mean to touch.
- Do **not** use `_expand=auto_order.steps`.  If `steps` is present in the update it replaces the item's steps.
  Leaving it out leaves the steps alone.

What the customer sees: the allowed frequencies are offered on the auto order item in MyAccount.  A change takes effect
after the next shipment; the next shipment date does not move.

**Step 1. Read the item with its auto order section \[[Create API Key](https://ultracart.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ucdoc/pages/38688545/API+Simple+Key)\]**
```bash
curl -X GET "https://secure.ultracart.com/rest/v2/item/items/merchant_item_id/AUTOSHIP-30?_expand=auto_order&_placeholders=false" \
  -H "Accept: application/json" \
  -H "X-UltraCart-Api-Version: 2017-03-01" \
  -H "x-ultracart-simple-key: 55f7c4940f843d01a10c5d77f17001009dcc02345e79bd01a10c5d77f1700100"
```

**Response Body** (abbreviated: check these fields)
```json
{
    "item": {
        "merchant_item_oid": 123456,
        "merchant_item_id": "AUTOSHIP-30",
        "auto_order": {
            "auto_orderable": true,
            "auto_order_upsell": true,
            ...
        },
        ...
    },
    "success": true
}
```

If `auto_order` is missing or `auto_order_upsell` is not `true`, the item does not use automatic enrollment.  Stop here.

**Step 2. Save the item with the frequencies a customer may switch to**

Send back the whole item from step 1 with the three properties added to `auto_order`.  Everything else in `auto_order`
goes back exactly as it was read.

```bash
curl -X PUT "https://secure.ultracart.com/rest/v2/item/items/123456?_expand=auto_order&_placeholders=false" \
  -H "Accept: application/json" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8" \
  -H "X-UltraCart-Api-Version: 2017-03-01" \
  -H "x-ultracart-simple-key: 55f7c4940f843d01a10c5d77f17001009dcc02345e79bd01a10c5d77f1700100" \
  -d $'{
    "merchant_item_oid": 123456,
    "merchant_item_id": "AUTOSHIP-30",
    "auto_order": {
        "auto_orderable": true,
        "auto_order_upsell": true,
        "auto_order_myaccount_frequency_schedules": ["Monthly", "Every 2 Months", "Every 3 Months"],
        "auto_order_myaccount_frequency_day_counts": [30, 60, 90],
        "auto_order_myaccount_frequency_last_step_only": false,
        ...
    },
    ...
}'
```

To turn the change off for the item, send `"auto_order_myaccount_frequency_schedules": []` and
`"auto_order_myaccount_frequency_day_counts": []`.

**Response Body** (abbreviated)
```json
{
    "item": {
        "merchant_item_oid": 123456,
        "merchant_item_id": "AUTOSHIP-30",
        "auto_order": {
            "auto_order_upsell": true,
            "auto_order_myaccount_frequency_schedules": ["Monthly", "Every 2 Months", "Every 3 Months"],
            "auto_order_myaccount_frequency_day_counts": [30, 60, 90],
            "auto_order_myaccount_frequency_last_step_only": false,
            ...
        },
        ...
    },
    "success": true
}
```

**Error Response Bodies**

The account does not have the feature enabled:
```json
{
    "error": {
        "developer_message": "auto_order.auto_order_myaccount_frequency_* can not be set because the advanced auto order settings are not enabled on this account.  Please contact support.",
        "user_message": "auto_order.auto_order_myaccount_frequency_* can not be set because the advanced auto order settings are not enabled on this account.  Please contact support."
    },
    "success": false
}
```

Other 400s: the item does not use automatic enrollment, an unknown schedule name, a day count outside 1 to 365, or more
than 20 day counts.

**Many items**

Repeat steps 1 and 2 for each item, one at a time, so each item gets its own result.  `PUT /item/items/batch` can take
up to 20 items per call, but it saves them in order and stops at the first one that fails, leaving the earlier ones
saved.  Without code, use the Batch Item Update tool (the MyAccount Frequency Change option).
